<h2>Context</h2>
<p>
  Two conflicting command-line designs existed in the initial repository snapshot:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>The legacy <code>CliApp</code> prototype referenced an early <code>System.CommandLine</code> 2.0 beta package that no longer restored (<code>CODE_AUDIT.md</code> A-18).</li>
  <li>Seven concept files in <code>FluxEncoderEngine/</code> subclassed <code>Spectre.Console.Cli</code> command types whose <code>ExecuteAsync</code> signatures no longer matched current <code>Spectre.Console.Cli</code> releases.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Because FluxEncoder targets single-binary and NativeAOT distribution, reflection-heavy command discovery is unsuitable: <code>Spectre.Console.Cli</code> discovers commands and settings via reflection over generic type arguments and attributes, generating trimming warnings and requiring manual dynamic-code preservation under NativeAOT. Conversely, <code>System.CommandLine</code> 2.0 is stable, maintained alongside the .NET SDK, and engineered to run trimmed and under NativeAOT.
</p>

<h2>Decision</h2>

{{ specTable({
  caption: "ADR 0002 ARCHITECTURAL & DEPENDENCY CLAUSES",
  headers: ["Area", "Policy Specification"],
  codeCols: [0],
  rows: [
    ["1. Parsing", "<code>System.CommandLine</code> 2.0 owns command, option, and argument parsing, help generation, and handler invocation. One root command tree is built in <code>FluxEncoder.Cli.CliApplication</code>."],
    ["2. Rendering", "<code>Spectre.Console</code> is used exclusively for terminal rendering (tables, progress displays, markup). <code>Spectre.Console.Cli</code> is never referenced."],
    ["3. Central Package Management", "<code>Directory.Packages.props</code> declares every package version with transitive pinning enabled. Project files (<code>.csproj</code>) declare <code>PackageReference</code> items without version attributes."],
    ["4. Committed Lock Files", "Every project commits <code>packages.lock.json</code>. Builds with <code>ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true</code> restore in <code>--locked-mode</code> and fail immediately on dependency drift."],
    ["5. Stable Releases Only", "Prerelease packages are prohibited. New package versions are adopted only after at least 14 days of public availability."],
    ["6. Vulnerability Auditing", "NuGet audit runs on direct and transitive dependencies at severity <code>low</code> and above. With warnings treated as errors, any advisory fails the build."],
    ["7. Testing Platform", "<code>xunit.v3</code> runs on <code>Microsoft.Testing.Platform</code> (configured in <code>global.json</code>). Test projects compile as self-hosting executables."]
  ]
}) }}

